rsx draw engine: the texture cache's size (RSX_DRAW_ENGINE_TEXTURE_CACHE) may be defined at build time.

A frame of Resistance 3's Haven street fight binds about 1700 distinct textures (world DXT textures up to 1024x1024
with nine levels, effect atlases, volumes). The engine's cache holds 1024, so every frame evicted and re-created
about 700 of the textures it was about to bind again (686 and 721 misses a frame on average in two runs, against
about 8000 hits): 22 ms of the RSX thread's CPU time a frame went to the texture cache, and the thread, the one the
fight waits on, spent 68 ms of CPU a frame. The default stays 1024; the port defines 2048 from its own build, like
SPU_WORKLOAD_MAX. The Metal backend's object table, which holds the textures besides targets, views and per-draw
copies (a released one until the command buffer that may use it is encoded), is sized from the cache: 2048 + twice
the cache, 4096 as before at the default.

Measured (scripted boot to the fight, 30 s standing in it, thread CPU time of the present thread per frame, two runs
each, other processes loading the machine alike): 1024 -> 686/721 misses, 22.5/22.9 ms in the cache, 68.0/68.1 ms
thread CPU, 1499/1571 frames presented; 2048 -> 1/1 misses, 5.0/3.8 ms, 45.1/41.0 ms, 2250/2641 frames.

tools/test_rsx_immediate_vertices.py builds test_rsx_draw_engine a second time with -DRSX_DRAW_ENGINE_TEXTURE_CACHE=2048
and -DRSX_TEST_EXPECT_TEXTURE_CACHE=2048: the test asserts the size it was built with, and the eviction test finds the
boundary at 2048. Without the change that build fails the assertion (1024 == 2048). Passes with clang and gcc.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_draw_engine.h b/libs/video/rsx_draw_engine.h
index 4ec4abd..1ee76a7 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_draw_engine.h
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_draw_engine.h
@@ -108,4 +108,9 @@ typedef struct rsx_be_render_state {
  * least recently used one. Public so the eviction test can be exact about
- * where the boundary is rather than assuming a number. */
+ * where the boundary is rather than assuming a number. A title whose frame
+ * binds more defines a larger cache at build time
+ * (-DRSX_DRAW_ENGINE_TEXTURE_CACHE=N): past the cap every frame evicts and
+ * re-decodes the textures it is about to bind again. */
+#ifndef RSX_DRAW_ENGINE_TEXTURE_CACHE
 #define RSX_DRAW_ENGINE_TEXTURE_CACHE 1024
+#endif
 
diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
index 31ec760..cafdd40 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
@@ -2200,3 +2200,6 @@ static void release_surfaces(void)
 
-#define ENG_MAX_OBJECTS  4096
+/* Textures share the table with targets, views and per-draw copies, and a
+ * released one keeps its slot until the command buffer that may use it is
+ * encoded: room for twice the engine's texture cache besides. */
+#define ENG_MAX_OBJECTS  (2048 + 2 * RSX_DRAW_ENGINE_TEXTURE_CACHE)
 #define ENG_MAX_PIPES    4096
